            {
              "text": "When administering a deceased estate in Brisbane’s Western Suburbs, you can engage a dedicated succession law specialist nearby or work with a local suburban firm familiar with the Centenary and Indooroopilly communities. \n\nFirms that specialize in Queensland probate and deceased estate administration in and around the Indooroopilly and Centenary areas include:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Dedicated Estate Specialists (Inner-West / Toowong Corridor)\n\n*   **Cornford-Scott Lawyers (Toowong Centrus)**\n    *   **Location:** 41 Sherwood Road, Toowong (minutes from Indooroopilly).\n    *   **Focus:** Consistently ranked by *Doyle’s Guide* as one of Queensland’s top-tier specialist succession and estate law firms. \n    *   **Best for:** Estates involving complex assets, business interests, potential family disputes/contested wills, or executors wanting specialist succession practitioners.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Centenary Suburbs (Jindalee & Mount Ommaney)\n\n*   **Jindalee Lawyers (Jindalee)**\n    *   **Location:** Centenary Suburbs / Jindalee.\n    *   **Focus:** Routine estate administration, applying for Grants of Probate and Letters of Administration in the Supreme Court of Queensland, and assisting personal representatives through executor duties.\n    *   **Best for:** Local, face-to-face appointments if you live in or around Jindalee, Westlake, Mount Ommaney, or Riverhills.\n\n*   **Steadfast Solicitors (Mount Ommaney / Jindalee)**\n    *   **Location:** Mount Ommaney area.\n    *   **Focus:** Boutique practice assisting executors with the formal probate process, asset gathering, creditor notification, and final distributions.\n    *   **Best for:** Personalized local service with flexible consultations.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Indooroopilly & Kenmore Area\n\n*   **Clear Legal (Indooroopilly)**\n    *   **Location:** Indooroopilly.\n    *   **Focus:** Suburban practice handling deceased estate administration, probate applications, and property transmissions following a death.\n    *   **Best for:** Accessible, straightforward assistance directly within the Indooroopilly shopping/business hub.\n\n*   **Crowley Greenhalgh Solicitors (Kenmore)**\n    *   **Location:** 18 Brookfield Road, Kenmore (just past Indooroopilly/Chapel Hill).\n    *   **Focus:** Established local firm with decades in the Western Suburbs advising executors on probate, asset distributions, and estate compliance.\n    *   **Best for:** A traditional, relationship-driven firm close to the Indooroopilly boundary.\n\n*   **Hawthorn Cuppaidge & Badgery Lawyers (Kenmore)**\n    *   **Location:** Kenmore.\n    *   **Focus:** One of Queensland’s oldest law practices, providing dedicated probate, letters of administration, and asset transmission services for personal representatives.\n\n---\n\n### Key Questions to Ask When Selecting a Firm\n\n1. **Scope of Engagement:** \n   * Do you only want them to obtain the **Grant of Probate** (leaving you to collect and distribute the bank accounts/assets yourself)?\n   * Or do you need **full estate administration** (handling estate bank accounts, advertising for creditors, tax compliance, and distributions)?\n2. **Fee Structure:** \n   * Many firms offer a **fixed fee** for standard Supreme Court probate applications (plus out-of-pocket court filing and advertising outlays). \n   * Full estate administration is usually billed by time or on an agreed stage-by-stage basis.\n3. **Queensland Protection Periods:**\n   * Ensure your chosen solicitor advises you on executor liability under the *Succession Act 1981 (Qld)*—specifically the statutory notice periods and the **6-month notice / 9-month filing window** for family provision claims before you distribute estate assets.",
